{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     RESERVED NAME: Ghost renders this from the {{navigation}} helper, never
     from {{> navigation}}. It is therefore the only place the site's
     navigation markup exists.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     ONE PARTIAL, THREE SURFACES. Ghost's navigation helper forwards any
     attribute passed to it onto the context, so `{{navigation variant="sheet"}}`
     arrives here as {{variant}}. That is what lets the bar, the mobile sheet
     and the footer share one source of navigation markup instead of three
     copies that quietly disagree about which link is current — the drift
     `abstract/10` is a record of.

     This file used to emit only <li> items so the caller could pick the <ul>.
     That was the right instinct with the wrong mechanism: the three surfaces
     need different ELEMENTS, not just a different wrapper — the sheet's rows
     are <a> with a mono index and a chevron, not list items at all.

     `aria-current="page"` rather than a class: the CSS keys off the same
     attribute a screen reader announces, so the highlighted item and the
     announced item cannot drift apart. Ghost computes `current` server-side,
     which is why the underline in the bar is correct with JavaScript off.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}

{{#match variant "sheet"}}

    {{#foreach navigation}}
        <a class="ns-navsheet__link" href="{{url absolute="true"}}"{{#if current}} aria-current="page"{{/if}}>
            {{!-- Mono index — the same numbering device NSDS uses in lists and
                  curricula, which makes the site map read as a table of
                  contents. Padded to two digits so the column stays straight;
                  `match` takes a comparison operator, which is the only way to
                  do arithmetic in a Ghost template. --}}
            <span class="ns-navsheet__index">{{#match @number "<" 10}}0{{/match}}{{@number}}</span>
            {{label}}
            <i class="ph ph-caret-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </a>
    {{/foreach}}

{{else match variant "footer"}}

    {{!-- sections.css styles `.ns-footer__col ul`, so the footer variant needs
          no class of its own — it only has to be a <ul> inside the column. --}}
    <ul>
        {{#foreach navigation}}
            <li><a href="{{url absolute="true"}}"{{#if current}} aria-current="page"{{/if}}>{{label}}</a></li>
        {{/foreach}}
    </ul>

{{else}}

    <ul class="ns-topnav__links">
        {{#foreach navigation}}
            <li><a href="{{url absolute="true"}}"{{#if current}} aria-current="page"{{/if}}>{{label}}</a></li>
        {{/foreach}}
    </ul>

{{/match}}
